      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MONT SAINT MICHEL (2) made nice improvement second up onto turf at Bairnsdale, coming from well back in the run to grab second in a BM56. 1100m looks a nice spot for him and this looks a good race for him. BRING THE THUNDER (1) is a danger. He ran a much better race last start at Moe when closing off well for second, beaten a long neck. He's still sparingly raced and Shinn goes on which helps. RANAKYE (3) hasn't really fired in two runs this time in but is better than that. He'd like it drier, watch conditions. ELLY DEE (7) was solid fresh in the same race as MONT SAINT MICHEL and should strip fitter. She maps for a soft trail. LISTENING IS DOING (4) is a chance on the latest effort in a bunched finish.",
